      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department name: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- course level: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL\n- degree granting: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- total units: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- unique courses: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\n- minimum total units: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\n- design units: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DESIGN_UNITS\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- subject id: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- regular terms: ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor each department name and course level where the course is degree granting and the total units are greater than 6, and for each academic year and subject in that department, provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, number of courses where the design units are at least 3, academic year, academic year description, subject ID, total units for the subject, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms in that department and year, and the deviation of each subject's total units from the department's average in that year. Do not return any rounded answers."
